# CTFd Boundary Rules

- Reuse CTFd for commodity features where practical: users, challenges, flags, teams, scoreboard, admin and CTF event mechanics.
- Prefer CTFd plugins, themes, APIs and adapters over invasive core modifications.
- Keep custom QuantaHub domain concepts behind clear modules/adapters.
- CTFd must not own the cyber-range isolation boundary.
- CTFd must never receive Docker socket, container runtime, hypervisor or unrestricted runner privileges.
- The Lab Orchestrator remains separately deployable and separately permissioned.
- Normal learning workflows may use QuantaHub-native modules instead of forcing every room/path through CTFd.
